; Nepply-specific Setup messages. Paired with Inno Setup's own language file in
; Nepply.iss [Languages]; keep every key present in every language.

[CustomMessages]
UpdateNotExited=Nepply has not exited safely. No update was installed. Close Nepply and retry.
UpgradeAppRunning=Nepply is still running and owns your Desktop icons. Close Nepply and retry. No update was installed.
UpgradeRecoveryDeferred=Setup could not restore your Desktop icons right now. The update will continue and Nepply restores them when it next starts. If they stay hidden, right-click the Desktop and choose View > Show desktop icons.
UninstallAppRunning=Nepply is still running and owns your Desktop icons. Close Nepply and try again. No application files have been removed.
UninstallRecoveryFailed=Nepply could not restore your Desktop icons automatically. Windows may have blocked Nepply.exe; do not disable protection. You can still uninstall: afterwards, right-click the Desktop and choose View > Show desktop icons (icons also return after you sign out and back in).%n%nContinue uninstalling?
LanguageId=en
WelcomeText=Nepply keeps your Desktop items and system stats in a panel at the edge of the screen.%n%nMove the pointer to the edge to open it. Setup needs no administrator rights.
FinishedText=Nepply is ready and sits in the system tray.%n%nMove the pointer to the edge of the screen to open the panel.
TaskStartup=Start with Windows
TaskGroupStartup=Startup:
UninstallRemoveData=Also remove Nepply's settings and logs?%n%nChoose No if you plan to reinstall and want to keep your settings.
